/-!
# FraCaS problem representation

Structures for FraCaS-style NLI problems (Cooper et al. 1996, as
transcribed by MacCartney into `fracas.xml`, vendored at
`FraCaS/Data/fracas.xml`; see `FraCaS/Data/SOURCE.md`).
`FraCaS/Data/Problems.lean` (generated by `scripts/gen_fracas_problems.py`
from the vendored XML, not hand-written) instantiates one `Problem` per
FraCaS id. This file is just the target shape and the `fracas_NNN`
theorem-emission step per Phase 2 of the README's roadmap is still ahead
— `Problem` values are data, not yet formalized MTT statements.
-/
namespace FraCaS

/-- `undef` covers the 41 problems whose source answer wasn't literally
"Yes"/"No"/"Don't know" (MacCartney's `fracas_nonstandard` cases) — kept
distinct from `unknown` (a genuine three-valued "don't know" answer)
rather than conflating the two. -/
inductive Answer
  | yes | no | unknown | undef
  deriving Repr, DecidableEq

/-- One FraCaS problem: numbered premises, a hypothesis, and the gold
answer. Four problems in MacCartney's XML (276, 305, 309, 310) have an
empty `<h>`/`<q>` (confirmed by parsing the vendored file directly — the
source document's own four problems with "missing questions altogether")
and are skipped by the generator rather than force-fit into this shape;
342 of 346 are populated. -/
structure Problem where
  id : Nat
  premises : List String
  hypothesis : String
  answer : Answer

end FraCaS
